---
description: JavaScript house conventions - apply when creating or editing plain JS files.
globs: "**/*.js,**/*.jsx,**/*.mjs,**/*.cjs"
alwaysApply: false
---

Editing JavaScript - load `javascript`: the FIRST action after this rule attaches is that Skill call, before the NEXT edit lands (a path-scoped rule attaches ON the touch, so it can never precede its own trigger) - skip the load when it is
already in context (some seats preload it); conventions are the source of truth, not recall. Name the skill you loaded, or say it was already in context - the receipt is what makes the load happen. It is the
base-language layer; the type layer (`typescript`, for checked JS) and framework layers stack on
top where installed. Skip one-line tweaks.
